<section image-layout="blank" id="r-iyNAiZx9"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="IH7ER1-PvG" vertical-align="start" colspan="38"><p role="eyebrow">Retrieval practice</p><h2>Can you reconstruct the movement without reciting a formula?</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 14pt;"><grid-item id="xP0LANAB5j" padding="6pt 0"><p font-size="17pt"><b>Test the promise.</b> What did “no speaking rules” promise, and how did the practice defeat that promise?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="EFyKBtpHdp" padding="6pt 0"><p font-size="17pt"><b>Track what survives.</b> What was canceled, what right was preserved, and how was participation transformed?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="8gNElDXWBU" padding="6pt 0"><p font-size="17pt"><b>Ask who can answer back.</b> Why must recognition involve another independent person, and how can social forms enable agency?</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="7YjKiYNVE1" background-color="palette-2" padding="10pt 16pt"><p font-size="17pt"><b>Final takeaway:</b> freedom is not the absence of every constraint; it is agency enabled through reciprocal, revisable social relations.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="BWxyouTVgn" padding="0" colspan="22"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/xMdx3Jcl4CCDiSLmiJVws.png" saved-media-id="yzs06pimuthecrb" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="dialectical-paper-assemblage" alt="Editorial cut-paper assemblage photographed on warm ivory paper (#FAF4E8), with crisp folded planes, subtle paper fiber and long soft daylight shadows, using vermilion #A13D32, blue slate #345F67 and ochre #B3822D with carbon-black details, no text or lettering. A vermilion path carries an ochre fragment through an open folded threshold and becomes two reciprocal blue-slate arcs between independent mirrored profiles." meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid><box type="content" x="650" y="72" w="260" h="82" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 10pt 14pt; border-left: 5pt solid var(--accent-color); border-radius: 4pt;"><p role="eyebrow">Checkpoint 01</p><h4>Promise → internal tension</h4></box><box type="content" x="650" y="224" w="260" h="82" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 10pt 14pt; border-left: 5pt solid rgb(179, 130, 45); border-radius: 4pt;"><p role="eyebrow">Checkpoint 02</p><h4>Cancel → preserve → transform</h4></box><box type="content" x="650" y="376" w="260" h="82" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 10pt 14pt; border-left: 5pt solid rgb(52, 95, 103); border-radius: 4pt;"><p role="eyebrow">Checkpoint 03</p><h4>Independence → reciprocity</h4></box></section>